              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "15554961"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Effector proteins function to alter host cell physiology and promote bacterial survival in host tissues. Contributes to the formation of Salmonella-induced filaments (Sifs) in infected epithelial cells and to replication in macrophages"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
      "note": {
        "texts": [
          {
            "value": "Secreted via type III secretion system 2 (SPI-2 T3SS), and delivered into the host cell. Membrane-associated. Localizes to the Salmonella-containing vacuole (SCV) in infected cells and to late endocytic compartments in transfected cells"
          }
        ]
      },
